Golden index-buffer hashes (FNV-1a over the 640x480 index surface, seeded scene,
camera walking SouthEast): progress 0   -> 0xd3ca1c79f13f69b6,
64 -> 0x90d157a95cf0c46d, 128 -> 0x8107c5511ed6566d.

Parity method for the goldens: the row walks were transcribed line-by-line from
scrollrt.cpp:957-980 / :1001-1042 / :1090-1114 into a throwaway simulator
(/tmp/model.py) that draws the same twelve layers into the same surface; the Go
port and the simulator agree bit-for-bit on all three progresses. The
simulator is NOT checked in and no test depends on it.

